  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#dom-location-hash is straightforward; the fragment should be set to null and we invoke the navigate algorithm. Step 6 in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#navigate is interesting, however, since it specifically excludes the case where the resource has a null fragment. As written, it appears that using `location.hash = \"\"` should effectively reload the current page, but none of Firefox, Safari, or Chrome appear to demonstrate this behaviour in http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4151.\n",
